WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.314
Here's why this matters: the series
moves four populations to the cloud,

2
00:00:05.314 --> 00:00:08.763
each on its own track, and
Book 03 is the HR track.

3
00:00:08.763 --> 00:00:09.887
It's about people.

4
00:00:09.887 --> 00:00:14.483
Every employee account follows the HR
record, and every contractor account

5
00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:19.225
follows the contractor source of authority,
which the agency still has to name.

6
00:00:19.225 --> 00:00:24.012
Then joining, moving and leaving
change access by rule, with no ticket.

7
00:00:24.012 --> 00:00:29.128
You'll know you're there when every enabled
account matches an authoritative record

8
00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:31.979
or an owned exception,
and every group that came

9
00:00:31.979 --> 00:00:35.049
from an organizational unit
(OU) is a validated rule.

10
00:00:35.049 --> 00:00:37.997
Devices and servers are Book 05,

11
00:00:37.997 --> 00:00:43.212
and service accounts and AI
agents are Books 02, 06 and 17.

12
00:00:43.212 --> 00:00:45.037
HR never describes those.

13
00:00:45.037 --> 00:00:47.570
Now, how identity gets built today.
